hadiths[1]{hadithnumber,text}:
"2958","**\nNarrated to us Muhammad ibn Bashshar, narrated to us Ibn Abi 'Adiyy, informed us Muhammad ibn Ishaq, who narrated to me Abu 'Ubaydah ibn 'Abdullah ibn Zam'ah, from his father and from his mother Zaynab bint Abi Salamah, from Umm Salamah (RA), who narrated it all from her. She said:\n\n\When it was my night in which the Messenger of Allah (ﷺ) came to me after the evening of the Day of Sacrifice (Yawm al-Nahr)"","" he came to me. Wahb entered upon me with a group of men from the family of Abu Umayyah"","" wearing garments over their heads. The Messenger of Allah (ﷺ) said to Wahb: 'Have you performed the Tawaf al-Ifadah yet"","" O Abu 'Abdullah?'\n\nHe replied: 'No"","" by Allah"","" O Messenger of Allah.'\n\nThe Prophet (ﷺ) said: 'Then remove the garment.'\n\nSo Wahb removed it from his head"","" and his companion removed his garment from his head.\n\nThey asked: 'Why is that"","" O Messenger of Allah?'\n\nHe (ﷺ) said: 'This is a day in which you have been permitted"","" if you have stoned the Jamrah (the pillars at Mina)"","" to remove all restrictions that were placed upon you"","" except for women. But if you remain in Ihram until evening before you perform Tawaf around this House (the Ka'bah)"","" you will return to the state of Ihram as you were before stoning the Jamrah.'\"""""""
